### Test - Create Patient with Missing Fields (Should Return 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User"
}

###

### Test - Create Patient with Invalid Email Format (Should Return 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "invalid-email-format",
  "phoneNumber": "+201234567890",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-15",
  "address": "Test Address"
}

###

### Test - Create Patient with Invalid Date Format (Should Return 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+201234567890",
  "dateOfBirth": "15/05/1990",
  "address": "Test Address"
}

###

### Test - Create Patient with Duplicate Email (Should Return 409)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another User",
  "email": "ahmed.mohamed@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+201111111111",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-03-20",
  "address": "Another Address"
}

###

### Test - Update with Duplicate Email (Should Return 409)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/patients/{{patientId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "existing.email@example.com"
}

###
